From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@heinemeierhansson.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:11:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Resume runtime PM before reconfiguring
 the PHY

Type-C orientation and mode callbacks (qmp_combo_typec_switch_set() and
qmp_combo_typec_mux_set()) call qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy() without holding
a runtime PM reference on the PHY device. When runtime PM is enabled for
the PHY via power/control=auto, an idle initialized PHY runtime-suspends,
entering autonomous mode and disabling/unpreparing its clocks including
pipe_clk.

A subsequent Type-C notification then runs qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy()
while the device is runtime-suspended: it accesses PHY registers with
clocks off and calls qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, true), which disables and
unprepares pipe_clk and the bulk clocks a second time (triggering
clk_core_disable / clk_core_unprepare warnings on gcc_usb3_prim_phy_pipe_clk
on the ASUS Zenbook A16 UX3607OA) and leaves the USB-C port wedged in
suspended state.

Resume the PHY device around qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy() with
pm_runtime_resume_and_get() / pm_runtime_put(), and guard
qmp_combo_runtime_suspend() and qmp_combo_runtime_resume() on
com_powered_on so a failed forced re-initialization cannot unbalance the
clocks on a later runtime PM transition either. Neither runtime PM callback
acquires phy_mutex, so resuming under phy_mutex cannot deadlock.
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 9eca19f..c23d131 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4900,6 +4900,10 @@ static int qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy(struct qmp_combo *qmp, enum qmpphy_mode new
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(qmp->dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	dev_dbg(qmp->dev, "qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy: switching from qmpphy mode %d to %d\n",
 		qmp->qmpphy_mode, new_mode);
 
@@ -4916,7 +4920,7 @@ static int qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy(struct qmp_combo *qmp, enum qmpphy_mode new
 	/* Now everything's powered down, power up the right PHYs */
 	ret = qmp_combo_com_init(qmp, true);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto out_put;
 
 	/* First USB4 initialization is performed once by usb4_init(). */
 	if ((qmp->usb_init_count || qmp->usb4_init_count) &&
@@ -4935,6 +4939,9 @@ static int qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy(struct qmp_combo *qmp, enum qmpphy_mode new
 	    qmp->dp_init_count)
 		qmp->cfg->dp_aux_init(qmp);
 
+out_put:
+	pm_runtime_put(qmp->dev);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -5191,7 +5198,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	dev_vdbg(dev, "Suspending QMP phy, mode:%d\n", qmp->phy_mode);
 
-	if (!qmp->init_count) {
+	if (!qmp->init_count || !qmp->com_powered_on) {
 		dev_vdbg(dev, "PHY not initialized, bailing out\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
@@ -5221,7 +5228,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 	dev_vdbg(dev, "Resuming QMP phy, mode:%d\n", qmp->phy_mode);
 
-	if (!qmp->init_count) {
+	if (!qmp->init_count || !qmp->com_powered_on) {
 		dev_vdbg(dev, "PHY not initialized, bailing out\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
-- 
